<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eichstätt</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eichstätt is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altmuhl">Altmühl</a> valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-boniface">Saint Boniface</a> made it a bishopric in the 740s under his kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willibald">Willibald</a>, and its prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> ruled the surrounding territory until 1802. Rebuilt in baroque style after the Swedish sack of 1634, it is now home to the Catholic University of Eichstätt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eichstatt.jpg" alt="Eichstätt" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Martin Geisler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eichst..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
